+
+#### Pruning finished branches and worktrees
+
+The `branches` group removes local branches (and the worktrees holding them) once their work has landed. It decides from the pull request state the VCS adapter reports, not from `git branch -d` or `git cherry`, so squash-merged branches are recognised even though their tip is not an ancestor of your default branch.
+
+```bash
+ta cleanup --only branches --dry-run   # Show each branch, its verdict and the reason
+ta cleanup --only branches             # Delete the safe ones, ask about the rest
+```
+
+A local branch is deleted without asking when its pull request is merged and the branch has no commits beyond the pull request head, or when its tip is already an ancestor of the default branch. It is never deleted when:
+
+- It is the current branch or the default branch.
+- It is checked out in a worktree with uncommitted or untracked files. You get a question that lists the files.
+- Its pull request is still open, it has no pull request, or it has commits beyond the pull request head. These are kept or raised as questions, never auto-deleted.
+- The adapter cannot tell its pull request state (kept, because unknown is not an answer).
+
+A worktree whose branch is finished is removed first (after a second cleanliness check), then the branch. Remote branches are never deleted. A remote branch whose pull request was closed without merging is listed as "report only".
+
+Every deletion is logged with the branch name and its tip SHA in `.ta/cleanup/branch-deletions.jsonl` and in `.ta/audit.jsonl`. To bring a branch back: `git branch <name> <sha>`.
+
+The group runs on its own right after `ta draft apply` observes the pull request merged (`ta draft watch`, or the merge step of apply), and in the daemon's periodic cleanup. Turn it off with:
+
+```toml
+# .ta/workflow.toml
+[cleanup]
+branches = false   # default true
